{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Is the goal to minimize the total cost (wages, overtime, and late-delivery compensation) while meeting all demand and training requirements, or is there a different objective such as maximizing profit or minimizing workforce size?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding the optimization objective, presenting alternatives within one sentence."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "When you say \"50 new workers must be trained by the end of the 8th week,\" does this mean that 50 trainees must have *completed* their 2-week training and become productive skilled workers by the end of week 8, or does it mean that 50 trainees must have *started* training by the end of week 8 (even if some are still in training)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy clarification regarding the definition of 'trained' (completion vs. start) by the deadline, which constitutes one independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Regarding the production capacity, is the 40-hour normal work week a hard limit that must be met exactly, or is it a baseline where workers can work fewer hours (e.g., 0 to 40 hours) without penalty, and overtime is only incurred if they exceed 40 hours up to the 60-hour maximum?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for the specific policy definition of the 40-hour work week (hard limit vs. baseline) and the conditions for overtime."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Regarding the wage structure, is the 540 yuan weekly wage for overtime the *total* weekly wage for a worker who works 60 hours (i.e., 360 yuan for the first 40 hours + 180 yuan for the 20 overtime hours), or is it an *additional* 540 yuan paid on top of the 360 yuan base wage for working overtime?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy clarification regarding the interpretation of the 540 yuan figure (total vs. additional), which constitutes one independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Regarding the training capacity constraint, is the limit of 3 new workers per skilled worker per two-week period a hard cap on the *total* number of trainees a single skilled worker can be responsible for at any given time, or is it a rate limit where a skilled worker can start training up to 3 new trainees in any rolling two-week window, potentially having more than 3 trainees in progress if they started in different windows?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response presents a single clarification question asking for a specific policy interpretation (hard cap vs. rate limit) regarding the training constraint."
}

